Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(bin): route POSIX -c probes to zsh in nu-login

Nushell is not POSIX, so callers that probe the login shell with
`$SHELL -l -i -c '<posix command>'` hit nu's parser and fail with
nu::parser::parse_mismatch, exiting 1. Cursor and VS Code do exactly
this to resolve the shell environment at startup, surfacing "Unable to
resolve your shell environment: Unexpected exit code from spawned shell
(code 1, signal null)".

Delegate any -c invocation, bare or clustered such as -lic, to the
existing zsh fallback and reserve nu for interactive login sessions.
Behavior is unchanged when no -c argument is present.

Verified: Cursor's env probe now exits 0 and resolves 182 variables
including the mise-managed PATH; shellcheck and shellharden are clean.

